    "lawCode": "Amd §7120, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3628\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to permitting foreign\ninsurance companies to transfer their corporate domicile to New York\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill would expand the scope of the existing insurer\nredomestication law (Section 7120 of the Insurance Law) to apply to\nnon-life insurance companies domiciled in another state, but\nauthorized to do insurance business in New York. Currently, the\nredomestication law applies only to foreign life insurance companies.\nUnder the bill, a foreign non-life insurance company that is\nauthorized in New York would have the ability to change its domicile\nto New York, with the approval of the New York Superintendent of\ninsurance and the ranking insurance official of the foreign non-life\ninsurer's current state of domicile.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends Section 7120 of the New York Insurance\nLaw to expand the scope of the existing redomestication law to allow\nany foreign insurance company authorized to do business in the State\nof New York to transfer its domicile to New York. The bill\naccomplishes this by deleting the word \"life\" and \"life insurance\" in\nthe appropriate places throughout Section 7120 of the Insurance Law.\nIn addition, Section 1 of the bill makes certain changes to Section\n7120 to use the Article 71 defined term \"company\" instead of \"insurer\"\nin a number of places.  Section 1 of the bill also clarifies that\ndifferent types of insurers, not only stock and mutual insurers, may\nredomesticate to New York under Section 7120.\n\nSection 2 of the bill establishes an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nNew York's strength in insurance regulatory matters makes it an\nattractive state for all insurers, including non-life insurers, to be\nbe domiciled. This bill sends a positive message to all types of\nforeign insurers that New York is an attractive state in which to do\nbusiness.\n\nCurrently, the process for a New York non-life insurance company to\nredomesticate to New York is extremely difficult.  It requires a\nforeign insurer to reincorporate in New York and merge the existing\ninsurer into the newly incorporated New York insurer.  This process is\nvery time-consuming and, in many states, requires the recently merged\nNew York insurer to obtain new licenses, agent appointments, and rate\nand policy form approvals.  Such procedures necessitate an overly\nburdensome and expensive regulatory process that does not benefit the\nState of New York.\n\nIn these difficult economic times, it is critical that measures be\ntaken by the Legislature to support economic development in New York.\nThis bill does that by expanding the types of insurers that may\nredomesticate to New York through a streamlined and more efficient\nprocess.  Eliminating non-functional impediments to the\nredomestication process will have a catalytic impact in encouraging\nall types of insurers to move to New York, thereby elevating the\npotential for the State to add new jobs and garner enhanced revenues.\nFurther, the bill will serve as yet another tool to maintain New\nYork's position as the worldwide center for the financial services\n\nindustry, and reaffirm the State's role as one of the leading\nregulators for the insurance industry.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNo known costs to the State are associated with this bill.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately upon being signed into law.\n",
